<h2>Weird Tales - 3rd Incarnation</h2>
Robert Weinberg and Victor Dricks bought the rights to the <i>Weird Tales</i> name when
Leo Marguiles died in 1975. The rights were then licensed to Lin Carter,
who persuaded Zebra Books to publish anthologies in paperback format with
the name. Four such books were produced before the attempt failed.

