<h2>Weird Tales</h2>

Initially a companion magazine to <i>Detective Tales</i>,
<i>Weird Tales</i> was the stomping grounds for H. P. Lovecraft,
with frequent contributions by Frank Belknap Long, August W.
Derleth, E. Hoffmann Price, Donald Wandrei, Robert Bloch, Henry
Kuttner, Clark Ashton Smith, and Robert E. Howard.

